{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014qSb5ajh34KJBL9JK5y7ao","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n99:Transient progress\n102:Normally when you exit the progress context manager (or call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.stop`) the last refreshed display remains in the terminal with the cursor on the following line. You can also make the progress display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Progress constructor. Here's an example::\n104:    with Progress(transient=True) as progress:\n108:Transient progress displays are useful if you want more minimal output in the terminal when tasks are complete.\n280:        for letter in track(\"ABCDEF\", transient=True):","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02877f4f-ce1d-4b36-9d84-b279a63f24e5","uuid":"ccb144ff-5c21-4755-a245-81d119a018cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:17:18.819Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\n99:Transient progress\n102:Normally when you exit the progress context manager (or call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.stop`) the last refreshed display remains in the terminal with the cursor on the following line. You can also make the progress display disappear on exit by setting ``transient=True`` on the Progress constructor. Here's an example::\n104:    with Progress(transient=True) as progress:\n108:Transient progress displays are useful if you want more minimal output in the terminal when tasks are complete.\n280:        for letter in track(\"ABCDEF\", transient=True):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014qSb5ajh34KJBL9JK5y7ao","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
